## Why This Is Asked

Assess ability to ground a feature in a measurable business case, translating product intuition into concrete cost and risk items for a mobile offline component.

## Key Concepts

- Offline-first architecture
- Inverted index vs suffix structures
- Delta sync and storage budgets
- Privacy/compliance and consent
- Rollout strategy and go/no-go criteria

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal indexing sketch (pseudo)
function indexDocs(docs) {
  const idx = {};
  for (const d of docs) {
    for (const t of tokenize(d.text)) {
      if (!idx[t]) idx[t] = [];
      idx[t].push(d.id);
    }
  }
  return idx;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure energy consumption during indexing and constrain it?
- How would you design delta-sync conflicts and eventual consistency across devices?

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests the ability to translate a complex edge-ML rollout into a precise 2-year CBA, balancing hardware, cloud costs, and real-world benefits like downtime and maintenance savings.

## Key Concepts

- Edge computing and on-device training
- Federated learning and privacy implications
- CAPEX vs OPEX modeling
- Downtime reduction and MTBF uplift as financial drivers
- Handling non-IID data and drift in multi-site deployments

## Code Example

```javascript
function estimateROI(capex, opexPerMonth, savingsPerMonth, horizonMonths) {
  const totalOpex = opexPerMonth * horizonMonths;
  const totalCost = capex + totalOpex;
  const totalSavings = savingsPerMonth * horizonMonths;
  const roi = (totalSavings - totalCost) / totalCost;
  return { totalCost, totalSavings, roi };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you monitor and mitigate model drift across sites?
- What metrics would you track to validate the ROI assumptions and trigger governance gates?

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates whether a candidate can translate a product feature into a tangible cost model, accounting for on-device constraints, privacy considerations, rollout strategy, and return on investment.

## Key Concepts
- On-device vs. cloud inference trade-offs
- Energy budgeting and latency SLA management
- Privacy regulations and user consent workflows
- Phased rollout strategies with cohort-based deployment
- Drift detection and model maintenance cycles

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode for CBA go/no-go decision
function evaluateGoNoGo(budget, savings) {
  const breakEvenMonth = calculateBreakEven(budget, savings);
  return {
    go: breakEvenMonth <= 12,
    breakEvenMonth,
    recommendation: breakEvenMonth <= 12 ? 'Proceed' : 'Reconsider'
  };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Assess understanding of privacy-preserving, on-device analytics and the viability of data-sharing via aggregates.

## Key Concepts

- On-device analytics and data minimization
- User consent and opt-in UX
- Aggregated data leakage risk and privacy controls
- Cost modeling: device runtime, memory, and backend bandwidth
- Rollout strategy, drift monitoring, and governance

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple rolling aggregate for 90-day window on-device
function rollingAvg(values, window=90) {
  let sum=0;
  const res=[];
  for(let i=0;i<values.length;i++){
    sum+=values[i];
    if(i>=window) sum-=values[i-window];
    if(i>=window-1) res.push(sum/(window));
  }
  return res;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate accuracy of aggregates vs server baselines?
- What are rollback or revocation strategies if consent changes mid-rollout?

